# =====================================================================
# Public-repo policy
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is PUBLIC and is scoped to what a supervisor needs to
# read and re-run the thesis pipeline:
#
#   README.md    orientation: thesis metadata, layout, how to run
#   src/ + pyproject.toml   the GS pricer the MC notebook imports
#   notebooks/   the three active notebooks (the analysis itself)
#   config/      JSON params the notebooks load at runtime
#   data/input/  the WTI panel + synthetic MC dataset the notebooks read
#   requirements.txt
#
# Everything else stays local. Adding a path here does NOT untrack a file
# that is already committed -- pair any new rule with `git rm --cached`.
# =====================================================================

# --- OS / editor junk ---
.DS_Store

# --- Python build & cache artefacts ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Model artefacts (regenerable by re-running the notebooks) ---
# Inputs under data/input/ ARE tracked: the WTI panel is not reproducible
# from code, and mc_data.pkl is what every result in the thesis is keyed to.
data/output/

# --- Figure outputs (regenerated by the local figure pipeline) ---
# Notebook figures render inline in the committed notebooks; nothing under
# figures/ needs to be in the public repo.
figures/

# --- Local-only code: standalone tooling, not part of the notebooks ---
scripts/

# src/ contributes exactly one tracked file: the closed-form Gibson-Schwartz
# pricer that monte_carlo_simulation.ipynb imports. Without it that notebook
# cannot run from a fresh clone. The import is a plain `from gs_wamol...`
# with no sys.path shim, so the package must be installed -- which is why
# pyproject.toml is tracked too. Everything else under src/ stays local, and
# the deny-then-allow shape below means anything NEW added under src/ is
# ignored by default rather than silently published.
src/*
!src/gs_wamol/
src/gs_wamol/*
!src/gs_wamol/physics/
src/gs_wamol/physics/*
!src/gs_wamol/physics/gibson_schwartz.py

# --- Thesis source and write-up (via the submission route, not GitHub) ---
# README.md carries the orientation a reader needs; the thesis itself, the
# working notes and the derivations PDF are all distributed separately.
*.tex
*.bib
*.pdf
docs/

# --- Development history (not supervisor-facing) ---
notebooks/archive/
